      },
      "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": "An ontology of histopathological morphologies used by pathologists to classify/categorise animal lesions observed histologically during regulatory toxicology studies. The ontology was developed using real data from over 6000 regulatory toxicology studies donated by 13 companies spanning nine species.\n\nThe original structure of the histopathology ontology was designed ab initio when the [INHAND](http://www.goreni.org/) manuscripts were not available. However, the ontology has been repetitively reviewed and updated to align with the subsequently published INHAND manuscripts. During this process cross references to INHAND lesion identifiers were added to the ontology. [from GitHub]",
