        "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370"
      },
      "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": "The Probes & Drugs portal (P&D) is a hub for the integration of high-quality bioactive compound sets enabling their analysis and comparison. Its main focus is on chemical probes and drugs but it also includes additional relevant sets from specialist databases/scientific publications, and vendor sets. Upon these, established bioactive chemistry sources (such as ChEMBL, BindingDB, Guide To Pharmacology, DrugCentral or DrugBank) are utilized for compounds' biological annotation.",
