      "@type": "https://bioregistry.io/schema/#0000001",
      "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": "The Pathogen Transmission Ontology describes the transmission methods of human disease pathogens describing how a pathogen is transmitted from one host, reservoir, or source to another host. The pathogen transmission may occur either directly or indirectly and may involve animate vectors or inanimate vehicles.",
