      "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": "DCAT-AP+ is a [LinkML](https://linkml.io/)-based extension of the [DCAT Application Profile 3.0](https://semiceu.github.io/DCAT-AP/releases/3.0.0/) that adds a provenance layer for describing how a dataset was generated and what it is about, using the [Starting Point Terms of PROV-O](https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/#description-starting-point-terms), the [QUDT ontology](https://www.qudt.org/), and [Dublin Core Terms](http://purl.org/dc/terms/). DCAT-AP+ is domain-agnostic. It provides a generic set of classes and properties that any domain can import and specialize into its own application profile. [ChemDCAT-AP](https://github.com/nfdi-de/chem-dcat-ap) is the first such domain profile, built for chemistry and catalysis research data.",
